# Exploration Report: WIP Picker fed by Department-Scoped BOM Components

## 1. `PlanningControlCenterClient.js` (`src/features/production-planning/components/`)

### `wipSkuCatalog` — prop chain & shape
Fetched via SWR at lines 244–258, **not** a prop — the page component fetches it directly:

```js
// line 245-249
const { data: skuCatalogData } = useSWR("/api/production-planning/schedule/sku-catalog", fetcher, ...);
// line 251-258
const wipSkuCatalog = useMemo(() => {
  const items = skuCatalogData?.data || [];
  return items.filter((item) =>
    String(item?.iccat_code || "").trim() === "03" ||
    String(item?.sku_code || "").startsWith("WIP"));
}, [skuCatalogData]);
```

**⚠️ Shape mismatch bug to be aware of:** the API (`src/app/api/production-planning/schedule/sku-catalog/route.js:150-166`) returns **camelCase** entries `{ skuCode, name, brand, unit, hasBom, formulaOptions, itemType }` — but the filter (line 255-256), the dropdown options (line 959-960 `sku.sku_code`), and `handleLineChange` (line 338-341 `sku.sku_code` / `matchSku.sku_name` / `matchSku.uom_name`) all read **snake_case** keys that don't exist in the response. So `iccat_code`/`sku_code` are always `undefined` and auto-fill never matches. Your new picker should use the API's actual camelCase fields (`skuCode`, `name`, `unit`, `itemType === "WIP"`).

### Section model — section → department mapping
`activeSection` (state, line 56) is one entry of `sectionOptions` (line 210), which comes from:

```js
// line 203-206
const sectionShiftKey = activeDeptId
  ? `/api/production-section-shifts?departmentId=${encodeURIComponent(activeDeptId)}` : null;
```

Each section object (built server-side in `src/lib/productionSectionShifts.js:85-99` `buildSectionShiftGroups`, sourced from `src/app/api/production-section-shifts/route.js:43-59`) has:

```js
{ id, name, displayOrder, templateId,
  departmentId, departmentCode, departmentName,   // ← section → department binding
  shifts: [{ shiftId, shiftCode, shiftName, startTime, endTime, ... }] }
```

Yes — a section maps to exactly one production department via `departmentId` (section defs live in `production_schedule_section_defs`, joined to departments through `production_schedule_templates.dept_id`). Note the page already selects the department first (`activeDeptId`, line 47) and fetches sections filtered by it, so `activeSection.departmentId === activeDeptId` in practice.

### `WipEditorModal` data flow & `handleLineChange`
- Defined at line 1296; rendered at line 1264-1276 with props `{ activeSection, sectionOptions, sectionRows, isLocked, wipSkuCatalog, getWipMeta, getShiftsForSection, handleLineChange, handleAddWipRow, handleRemoveWipRow, onClose }`. `sectionRows` = `draftLines` filtered to `activeSection` (lines 1133-1137, matching on `sourceSectionDefId`/`sourceSectionName`). It's a single minified JSX line (1297); the รหัส WIP cell renders a `<select>` whose onChange calls `handleLineChange(row.tempId, "skuCode", value)`.
- `handleLineChange` (lines 330-347): immutable-update of the `draftLines` local state entry by `tempId`; when `field === "skuCode"` it looks up the catalog and auto-fills `skuName` and `unit`:

```js
if (field === "skuCode") {
  const matchSku = wipSkuCatalog.find((sku) => sku.sku_code === value);
  if (matchSku) {
    updated.skuName = matchSku.sku_name || "";
    updated.unit = matchSku.uom_name || matchSku.uom || "kg";
